ut steps that the agent took during the call that are displayed to the next agent that takes the call. You can also use the <code>UpdateContactAttributes</code> operation to update attributes for a contact using data from your CRM application and save the data with the contact in Amazon Connect. You could also flag calls for additional analysis, such as legal review or identifying abusive callers.</p> <p>Contact attributes are available in Amazon Connect for 24 months, and are then deleted.</p> <p> <i>Important:</i> </p> <p>You cannot use the operation to update attributes for contacts that occurred prior to the release of the API, September 12, 2018. You can update attributes only for contacts that started after the release of the API. If you attempt to update attributes for a contact that occurred prior to the release of the API, a 400 error is returned. This applies also to queued callbacks that were initiated prior to the release of the API but are still active in your instance.</p>", "summary": null, "domain_schemas": ["AttributeValue", "UpdateContactAttributesResponse"], "name_tokens": ["update", "contact", "attributes"], "path_tokens": ["contact", "attributes"], "param_tokens": ["256", "algorithm", "amz", "content", "credential", "date", "headers", "security", "sha", "signature", "signed", "token", "x"], "schema_tokens": ["attribute", "attributes", "contact", "response", "update", "value"], "T": "[METHOD] post [NAME] update contact attributes [PATH] contact attributes [PARAMS] 256 algorithm amz content credential date headers security sha signature signed token x [SCHEMA] attribute attributes contact response update value"}, {"op_key": "POST /contact/stop", "method": "POST", "path": "/contact/stop", "operation_id": "StopContact", "param_names": ["X-Amz-Algorithm", "X-Amz-Content-Sha256", "X-Amz-Credential", "X-Amz-Date", "X-Amz-Security-Token", "X-Amz-Signature", "X-Amz-SignedHeaders"], "schema_names": ["ContactNotFoundException", "InternalServiceException", 